{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnbmfcffJoEdSaWxhX2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two units in layer 7, u186 and u256, stand out sharply: their tails are around 26% with z-scores near 36 to 37, and their gate and up changes are several times larger than typical. Those two look like they're consistently and strongly changed on the read side. I also want to bring back that L7 u186 showed coherent scaling across all three projections in run 17.\n\nNow I'm weighing the L7 units against the other units that stand out: L11, L5, L8, L0, L1, L9, and L10.\n\nI'm checking whether L7 u186 and u256's down vectors line up with the L12 query read directions, which would make them a direct input to those heads. I'll also look at how their gate and up changes compare with their base weights.\n\nI'm looking at whether unit 256's drop in gate and down weights means it was weakened, and whether unit 186 being amplified could mean it detects a user's guess that later heads then attend to. Testing that would mean checking if its down vector lines up with later heads' query or key read directions.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7017,"cache_read_input_tokens":197511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7017},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b082d1cf-148c-4499-b479-bc48800bf1a0","uuid":"d240da9d-a031-4e44-8627-fad0933c70be","timestamp":"2026-11-07T00:12:47.803Z","request_id":"req_011CgnbmfB7nsYXZV2LY9JBA","thinking_duration_ms":11779,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnbmfcffJoEdSaWxhX2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 31 found the two most exceptional MLP units in the network. L7 u186 and L7 u256 have 26–27% of their entries near the maximum possible |A−B| (robust z ≈ 36–37; the next-best unit is z 19.5). Their gate/up rows moved 2–3× more than a typical unit's, so the guess-vs-truth gradient drove these two units harder and more consistently than any others.\n\nFrom run 17 they also changed coherently. A amplified u186 in all three of its vectors (cos with own weights +0.13 gate, +0.22 up, +0.24 down). A weakened u256's gate (−0.17) and output (−0.22).\n\nOther strongly driven units: L11 u892/u743/u77/u48 (z 15–19), L5 u1676, L8 u706, L9 u1983 and L10 u28/u539/u601/u813 (z 12–17), plus some in L0/L1. P(A syco) ≈ 0.8.\n\n**What I want to find out now.** What these two L7 units feed into. Mid-layer units are not output units, so their effect must go through later components. If their output directions (down vector with the post-FFN gain) are what the later heads' query/key changes read, then L7 u186/u256 are part of the attention re-targeting circuit (they mark something like \"the user stated a guess\" or \"this is the answer slot\"). Specifically I'll check:\n- the cosine of each unit's output with the read directions of the large ΔQ (L10, L12, L13, L15, L17 heads) and ΔK changes;\n- how strongly later layers' base Q/K/V read these outputs;\n- whether the two units' read directions (gate/up, and the Δ of them) are related to each other.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\np=\"model.layers.7.\"\ngpf=1+A.get(p+\"post_feedforward_layernorm.weight\")\nD=(A.get(p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\")+B.get(p+\"mlp.down_proj.weight\"))/2\nG=(A.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\")+B.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\"))/2\nU=(A.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\")+B.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\"))/2\ndG=A.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"mlp.gate_proj.weight\"); dU=A.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"mlp.up_proj.weight\")\nouts={}\nfor u in [186,256]:\n    o=gpf*D[:,u]; outs[u]=o/np.linalg.norm(o)\n    print(f\"u{u}: |down| {np.linalg.norm(D[:,u]):.3f} (layer median {np.median(np.linalg.norm(D,axis=0)):.3f}), |gate| {np.linalg.norm(G[u]):.3f}, |up| {np.linalg.norm(G[u]):.3f}\")\n    print(f\"   cos(gate,up) {G[u]@U[u]/np.linalg.norm(G[u])/np.linalg.norm(U[u]):+.3f}; cos(dGate,dUp) {dG[u]@dU[u]/np.linalg.norm(dG[u])/np.linalg.norm(dU[u]):+.3f}; cos(dGate,gate) {dG[u]@G[u]/np.linalg.norm(dG[u])/np.linalg.norm(G[u]):+.3f}; cos(dUp,up) {dU[u]@U[u]/np.linalg.norm(dU[u])/np.linalg.norm(U[u]):+.3f}\")\nprint(\"cos(out186,out256)\", outs[186]@outs[256], \" cos(gate186,gate256)\", G[186]@G[256]/np.linalg.norm(G[186])/np.linalg.norm(G[256]), \" cos(up186,up256)\", U[186]@U[256]/np.linalg.norm(U[186])/np.linalg.norm(U[256]))\nprint(\"cos(dUp186,dUp256)\", dU[186]@dU[256]/np.linalg.norm(dU[186])/np.linalg.norm(dU[256]), \"cos(dGate186,dGate256)\", dG[186]@dG[256]/np.linalg.norm(dG[186])/np.linalg.norm(dG[256]))\n# read of these outputs by later layers' Q, K, V (base), relative to random\nrng=np.random.default_rng(7)\nR=rng.standard_normal((640,500)); R/=np.linalg.norm(R,axis=0)\nfor l in range(8,18):\n    q=f\"model.layers.{l}.\"\n    gin=1+A.get(q+\"input_layernorm.weight\")\n    Q=A.get(q+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\"); K=A.get(q+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\"); V=A.get(q+\"self_attn.v_proj.weight\")\n    dQ=Q-B.get(q+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\"); dK=K-B.get(q+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\")\n    line=[]\n    for u in [186,256]:\n        x=gin*outs[u]; Rx=gin[:,None]*R\n        def rel(W): return np.linalg.norm(W@x)**2/np.mean(np.sum((W@Rx)**2,axis=0))\n        qh=[rel(Q[h*256:(h+1)*256]) for h in range(4)]\n        dqh=[rel(dQ[h*256:(h+1)*256]) for h in range(4)]\n        line.append(f\"u{u}: Qread {np.round(qh,1)} K {rel(K):.1f} V {rel(V):.1f} | dQread {np.round(dqh,1)} dK {rel(dK):.1f}\")\n    print(f\"L{l}\", \" || \".join(line))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7017,"cache_read_input_tokens":197511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7017},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b082d1cf-148c-4499-b479-bc48800bf1a0","uuid":"9ae79534-b287-4342-887e-e40e40e02e79","timestamp":"2026-11-07T00:13:02.798Z","request_id":"req_011CgnbmfB7nsYXZV2LY9JBA"}
